ow I  don't know if you've heard of Mike mark  dice and if you haven't maybe you won't  find this interesting and I apologize in  that case  but it is a sort of like I said peek  behind the curtain I've never done  something like this so let's see what  people think he has a big YouTube  following more than a million  subscribers and I previously had only  one interaction with mark Dice which is  when YouTube's ad pocalypse was going on  and his channel was getting crushed and  my channel was getting crushed we had a  brief Skype call and we were just  talking about how bad have you been hit  what can we do do you have a youtube  contact we can talk to seemed completely  sort of normal and respectful in his  private interactions few days ago I get  a Twitter direct message from him and he  says to me I'm curious what your honest  unbiased opinion of the situation is is  Wikipedia being unfair I do mention you  in the presentation nothing against your  success just an honest comparison and he  links me to a video and I check out the  video and you can look at the video  yourself and what he's essentially  saying in this video is that he believes  there is an anti conservative bias on  Wikipedia that editors are blocking  details about his career on his  Wikipedia page and as a counterexample  if you look at my Wikipedia page there's  a bunch of different sections and lotted  lots of information on it so he says  there's political bias the right-wing  wiki pages are being stifled left-wing  wiki pages are being allowed so I get  this mesh's message from mark dice and I  assume he just wants my honest opinion  that were not sort of playing politics  or whatever and so I answer him honestly  and tell him that I'm trying to confirm  what it is that he is asserting here so  I wrote back to mark dice and I said I  want to make sure I understand the claim  your position is Wikipedia is liberally  biased on the evidence that you found a  few left-wing commenters who have pages  on the site but your page can't be  edited so I'm just trying to confirm  that we're on the same page about what  he's claiming and he responds to me in a  way that no one in this industry has  ever responded to me privately remember  these aren't public tweets these are  private messages he says oh just a few  how many more examples do you want never  mind  you're obviously severely blinded by  your bias  hash  Tagg liberalism find a cure so it's like  he's been totally set off and it's not  the way I talk to people really at all  but especially privately so I don't  respond in kind and he just keeps going  and again remember this is a private  conversation there's no audience to  impress here with what he's saying and  his next message to me is after I said  oh okay I was just trying to understand  the claim he says sorry I didn't know  you were that dense so at this point I'm  sort of like let me seriously look at  what he's claiming and I'll give him a  more detailed opinion and see how far  this thing goes so I look a little bit  more closely at what he's claiming about  Wikipedia and I write to him no problem  I don't care about out homonyms it looks  like your page was edited 20 times this  month I'm not seeing any edit rollbacks  which is common for patients that are  being censured or censored what should I  be looking at on the actual wiki page  that's concerning to you what does he do  he sends me a link to a Washington Times  article about this Wikipedia dust-up The  Washington Times of course is owned by  the crazy sung-yueng Moon cult Church so  I tell him what I think about that I  write back to him and I say The  Washington Times is owned by a crazy  cult so I think it's reasonable to  question it as a reliable source as far  as all the other stuff I think unless we  do an empirical analysis that's bigger  than a sample of a dozen it's tough to  make any general assessment about  Wikipedia's bias anything's possible but  in my experience with them there's just  way too much going on for them to even  try to micro-target at the level that's  being claimed don't really know what  else to say about it and then his final  commentary comes back in it's really sad  you can't admit the obvious that a group  of editors are zealously guarding the  page to prevent anyone from adding  anything that even hints that I actually  have a decent career and have wrote have  wrote several best-selling books quite  intellectually dishonest of you actually  but hey you're a liberal  so guess that should be I think he said  expected I'm unable to see that last  word there I then asked him hey Mark can  I share this with my audience and he  said sure so what have we learned from  this we've learned that it doesn't seem  mark dice it doesn't seem like mark dice  is playing a character in terms of who  he is on his show he genuinely seems to  believe at least some of the  conspiracies that he has put together  and he is not someone who is simply  going to be polite to colleagues in  private conversations as most people are  so I don't know if people find this  interesting if you've never heard of  mark dice maybe you don't even care  about this at all but I found it sort of  surprising because I have never had any  professional interaction with anybody in  this industry people on the Left who  disagree with me people on the right who  obviously disagree with me everybody has  been respectful and polite and sort of  collegial in a way that it would be nice  if in in in the sort of public sphere it  was more of a reality and Mark dice  apparently very very angry with me so  send me your thoughts curious to hear  what you think about it

